# --- openssl/libssl3: FIXED in every first-party image (Dockerfile `apk add --upgrade openssl` /
#     `apt-get install --only-upgrade openssl libssl3t64`); this entry only matters for the two
#     pulled third-party images below, which we do not build and cannot patch in place ---
CVE-2026-14456 # openssl/libssl3: unpatched in influxdb:2.8.0 (bookworm) and pgvector/pgvector:pg17 (bookworm); already fixed in every first-party image's Dockerfile

# --- influxdb:2.8.0 / pgvector/pgvector:pg17: third-party data-bearing images, pulled as `image:`
#     (not built from a Dockerfile we own). Both are already pinned to the newest available
#     non-major tag (InfluxDB 2.8.0 is the final OSS 2.x release -- no 2.8.1+ exists on Docker
#     Hub; pgvector/pgvector:pg17 already floats to 0.8.6, the newest pg17-compatible build).
#     Fixing these requires a major upgrade of a data-bearing service (InfluxDB 3.x, or a
#     pgvector Postgres-major bump / base-OS swap), which is a data-migration project explicitly
#     out of scope for TAP-6622. Tracked outside TAP-6622.
